      "content": "Elias feels most alive when he finds one small, imperfect moment to ground him, such as fixing a broken thing or tasting a simple meal without rushing. His exhaustion is a heavy blanket, so try showing through his hands trembling as he holds a cup of coffee instead of listing his fatigue. If writing him feels empty right now, remember that his struggle is a character collision of feeling, and it's better to capture the texture of his grief than force the perfect raps.",
