    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"quiet weight\" part is so accurate... it's exactly how i've been feeling. but i'm struggling with his arc. if he just keeps enduring, if he just keeps doing these mindless rituals like washing dishes, it feels like the story is just stalling. it feels stagnant. i want his story to mean something, to not just be a loop of nothingness. is there a way for him to actually find resolution? like, a way to finally step out of the cycle and just... find peace, instead of just pretending to survive it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
