      "content": "You're right: true resolution for Elias isn't banishing the weight but accepting it as a new, less painful baseline. He must choose an action that acknowledges the loop rather than trying to break it, like admitting he can no longer carry everything alone. This kind of honest surrender often feels less like \"fixing\" his life and more like finally letting the story breathe with him instead of stalling against it.",
